+ * the private user identity of its REGISTER, temporary until its registration completes (ipsec_set_completed()); a
+ * new challenge deletes the temporary sets of the same UE registration and a temporary set ends after its lifetime
+ * (TS 33.203 clauses 7.3.1 and 7.4.2a, TS 24.229 clause 5.2.2.2); ipsec_impi_reserve() admits a REGISTER under
+ * clause 7.1 rule 3 atomically with the count, ipsec_create() consumes the admission with the set and deletes a set
+ * it cannot record; after SM12 the old set stays in use for outbound messages until the UE's first message over
+ * the new one (clause 7.4.2a), ipsec_forward() sending over the set in use (responses over the set their request
+ * came on); ipsec_sa_pair_free() checks the records; ipsec_reply_over_sa() sends a stateful reply to a protected
+ * request over the set it came on (clause 7.1); a copy of a set that is gone no longer deletes or releases anything.
+ *
+ * Modified by OpenMCX on 2026-10-25 (GPL-2.0 section 2(a)): the Security-Server lists the P-CSCF's
+ * algorithm combinations; every SA and policy of a tunnel is checked and a failed tunnel is taken back; the SAs
+ * carry the unique-salt bits of TS 33.203 annex I.
